  The model-facing description in index.mjs reproduces

      codex-rs/apply-patch/apply_patch_tool_instructions.md
        at commit 88c7a4ff074df9e2161c947ca6d91bf824b9d6e6

  with four modifications and no others:

    1. The `## apply_patch` heading and the blank line after it are dropped.
    2. "Use the `apply_patch` shell command to edit files" reads "tool" instead
       of "shell command", because here it is a function tool taking one string
       argument.
    3. The trailing `You can invoke apply_patch like:` sentence and the
       `shell {"command":["apply_patch", ...]}` example are dropped, for the
       same reason.
    4. Non-ASCII punctuation is flattened: U+2011 non-breaking hyphens to `-`,
       U+201C/U+201D to `"`, U+2019 to `'`. Three lines are affected.

  The text is otherwise byte-identical, and every operation the grammar defines
  is implemented, so nothing in it describes something the tool refuses.

  parse-patch.mjs and codex-apply.mjs are ports — the same algorithms in
  JavaScript, not a translation of any one function line by line — of

      codex-rs/apply-patch/src/streaming_parser.rs   (`process_line`)
      codex-rs/apply-patch/src/parser.rs             (markers, `push_context_line`)
      codex-rs/apply-patch/src/seek_sequence.rs      (`seek_sequence`)
      codex-rs/apply-patch/src/file_update.rs        (`derive_new_contents_from_chunks`,
                                                      `compute_replacements`,
                                                      `apply_replacements`)
        all at commit a7edf37cb46b5fc4d50bd03df8e5999a86f602eb

  Only the `NormalizeToLf` update mode is ported. It is the `#[default]` for
  `ApplyPatchFileUpdateMode`; `PreserveLineEndings` is selected by an
  environment variable the model cannot set, and it is the only reason upstream
  carries `context_line_indices`, so the ported chunks do not record it.

  parse-patch.mjs also transcribes six productions of

      codex-rs/core/src/tools/handlers/apply_patch.lark
        at commit 88c7a4ff074df9e2161c947ca6d91bf824b9d6e6

  as a comment, for the reader; that is a transcription, not a copy of the file.

  codex-fixtures.json is generated output, not source: codex-oracle.mjs runs the
  released `codex` binary over a temporary tree for each case and records what
  it printed and what the tree became. Where a case was refused, the recorded
  text is the binary's own diagnostic. Regenerating it requires a `codex` on
  PATH and is not part of the build or the test run.

  The recorded run used codex-cli 0.147.0, whose apply-patch sources sit at tag
  rust-v0.147.0 rather than at the commit ported above. The two differ in these
  files by a refactor — `UpdateFileChunk::default`, `push_context_line`, and the
  `context_line_indices` field — plus one behavioural change in
  `seek_sequence`'s end-of-file start position that applies to
  `PreserveLineEndings` only. Under `NormalizeToLf` they are the same
  algorithms, which is why the fixtures and the port agree on every case.

  An earlier version of this file said the description also dropped
  `*** Delete File:` and `*** Move to:` and their grammar productions. That was
  true when written and stopped being true when both operations were
  implemented. It is recorded here because a modification notice that
  under-reports what was reproduced is the kind that matters.

